# Makes a piece of art in the Art Library from where render_screens_boot.b3t
# leaves Rock Band 3 Deluxe (the welcome hint, on a fresh profile): Customize,
# Customize Band, Edit Band Logo, Create New Art, one sticker as its only
# layer, then Finish Editing and Save Changes. Saving copies the art maker's
# render target into the new piece's own texture on the CPU
# (PatchPanel::CopyToPatch, PatchDir::CacheRenderedTex: DxTex::LockBitmap on
# the target, SetBitmap on the piece's texture), so the library's thumbnail
# and the clipboard's big preview after it show the pixels that copy got.
# LockBitmap untiles guest memory's copy of the target, and only a resolve
# puts the target's pixels there: under --renderer=native nothing does (the
# sync-only GPU draws nothing), nor under --renderer=emulated without
# --readback_resolve=fast or full. Until 2026-10-20 the piece was colourful
# noise (whatever the memory held, a different pattern each run), while the
# art maker's own clipboard and the save prompt's New thumbnail, drawn from
# the target itself, were right: art-maker-* right, art-library-new* noise
# was the bug. Under native, src/Hooks/bitmap_readback.cpp now draws the
# target again on the CPU from its recorded passes into the bitmap (the
# log's "Target readback:" line); under emulated without readback_resolve
# it's still noise.
#   python tools/band3ctl.py launch --fresh -- --renderer=native --test_random_seed=21 --async_shader_compilation=false
#   python tools/band3ctl.py run tests/game/render_screens_boot.b3t
#   python tools/band3ctl.py run tests/game/art_library.b3t
# The piece is saved in the profile with the pixels it was given and comes
# back so at the next launch, under either renderer.
# Screenshots are under screenshots/ next to the exe: art-* the window's
# picture, art-*-native the native renderer's drawing of the same moment
# (under --renderer=emulated, from the guest memory the emulated GPU reads).
# It leaves the game on the main menu.

# the welcome hint: Continue, to the main menu
wait screen=hint_rb3_welcome_screen timeout=30s
sleep 1s
press down
sleep 333ms
press green until screen=main_hub_screen timeout=30s
sleep 2s

# Customize, Customize Band, Edit Band Logo: the Art Library, empty but for
# No Art. From the band's practice space it's a screen of its own; after
# the art maker it's patch_select_screen
press down
sleep 333ms
press down
sleep 333ms
press down
sleep 500ms
press green
sleep 1s
press green until screen=manage_band_screen timeout=30s
sleep 1500ms
press down
sleep 500ms
press green until screen=patch_select_practice_space_screen timeout=30s
sleep 2s
screenshot art-library-empty

# Create New Art, the slot after No Art: the art maker (patch_screen)
press right
sleep 500ms
press green until screen=patch_screen timeout=30s
sleep 2s
# Add New Layer's first category (New York Adorned Tattoo) and its first
# sticker (the tree), which becomes Layer 1. The clipboard is the art maker's
# render target drawn live, right under either renderer
press green
sleep 2s
press green
sleep 2s
screenshot art-maker-layer
screenshot native art-maker-layer-native
# Finish Editing: the save prompt, with the old (blank) and new art
press red
sleep 2s
screenshot art-maker-save
screenshot native art-maker-save-native

# Save Changes: CopyToPatch runs, and the library comes back with the new
# piece chosen, its menu (Apply Art...) and the clipboard showing it
press green until screen=patch_select_screen timeout=30s
sleep 2s
screenshot art-library-new
screenshot native art-library-new-native
# back out of its menu: the library's thumbnail, the clipboard behind
press red
sleep 1500ms
screenshot art-library-new-closed
screenshot native art-library-new-closed-native

# back to the main menu
press red until screen=manage_band_screen timeout=30s
sleep 1500ms
press red until screen=main_hub_screen timeout=30s
sleep 1s
